{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008056-creating-npc-sheets-in-2ed","id":1008056,"title":"Creating NPC sheets in 2ED","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T06:46:09-08:00","id":1008056,"title":"Creating NPC sheets in 2ED","content":"I'm currently planning my first Chronicle, it takes place in London and it has a relatively large roster of characters, the thing is that I don't know how to create sheets for all the NPCs, do I use the same system? What about Elder or Ancillae characters? The recommend experience for each rank seems to be a little underwhelming and not really reliable for creating any real movers and shakers, so how do you do it? What is your method for creating NPC sheets?<br /> <br /> As a side note, any idea for how one can translate 1ED characters into 2ED mechanics? Say Persephone Moore or Augusto Vidal for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:30:38-08:00","id":1008142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008056-creating-npc-sheets-in-2ed#post1008056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently planning my first Chronicle, it takes place in London and it has a relatively large roster of characters, the thing is that I don't know how to create sheets for all the NPCs, do I use the same system? What about Elder or Ancillae characters? The recommend experience for each rank seems to be a little underwhelming and not really reliable for creating any real movers and shakers, so how do you do it? What is your method for creating NPC sheets?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. Okay, not really, I just use a variation of the Horror rules for most NPCs: figure out what they're good/bad at, then assign dicepools to those actions, with a third dicepool for everything else.<br /> If I <i>really</i> need a full, complete statblock for an NPC, I just eyeball it. Figure out which ratings the NPC should have in which abilities, and just ignore how much XP that should be.<br /> <br /> However, there's a good rule of thumb for Disciplines: take the square root of the NPC's active years. Active for 100 years? 10 dots of disciplines. 25 years? 5 dots. Granted, it breaks with less than 9 years' activity, but I can live with that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a side note, any idea for how one can translate 1ED characters into 2ED mechanics? Say Persephone Moore or Augusto Vidal for example. </div> </div> </div>Ctrl-C, Ctrl-V, plus Aspirations and Touchstones (if any).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:33:26-08:00","id":1008145,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't create full character sheets for my NPCs. I only write down what I need when I need it. The exception may be powers because I don't want to cheat my players. For most my NPCs I don't have a sheet or anything written down because it might never be useful. When I need something though, I make up the numbers as I see fit, according to the character's background and concept.<br /> <br /> For example, my ultra social elder vampire will never have any skill written down until she gets into a social confrontation with a PC. Then, and only then, I determine that she has 5 in Presence and 4 in Expression (because she is the ultra social elder vampire and it makes sense, relative to her concept).<br /> <br /> As a result, I would rather have a concept in mind for each of my NPCs rather than number. Numbers are derived from that concept when I need them. I don't care about experience points. They are only for PCs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Justin Sane beat me to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","user":"Lestat","date":". 11-25-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:48:24-08:00","id":1008243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lestat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008056-creating-npc-sheets-in-2ed?p=1008145#post1008145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello,<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't create full character sheets for my NPCs. I only write down what I need when I need it. The exception may be powers because I don't want to cheat my players. For most my NPCs I don't have a sheet or anything written down because it might never be useful. When I need something though, I make up the numbers as I see fit, according to the character's background and concept.<br /> <br /> For example, my ultra social elder vampire will never have any skill written down until she gets into a social confrontation with a PC. Then, and only then, I determine that she has 5 in Presence and 4 in Expression (because she is the ultra social elder vampire and it makes sense, relative to her concept).<br /> <br /> As a result, I would rather have a concept in mind for each of my NPCs rather than number. Numbers are derived from that concept when I need them. I don't care about experience points. They are only for PCs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Justin Sane beat me to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice, both of you, much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:25:12-08:00","id":1008695,"title":"","content":"I second (third ?) that. Most of my important NPCs didn't really have a character sheet, although I knew what they were supposed to be good at. In the very rare occasion when I had to roll dice for them, I just took a number of dice that seemed appropriate. I only made a character sheet for those that had a good chance of actually confronting the PCs (mostly meaning physical combat) and even then, most of the time, I just set a number of dots in the relevant areas : attributes, a few skills, BP, disciplines and the derived traits.<br /> <br /> Other than that, it might also be a good idea to have character sheet templates for generic NPCs. Thugs, civilians, cops, ghouls or even a random newly embraced vampire. For those, I'd use the regular character creation for the number of dots, maybe bonus one or two dots if they're supposed to be a bit more of a threat than average, but that's usually not necessary. It's a little bit of work, but that way, you have a couple of easy to use sheets for scenes involving unimportant NPCs and the action can run a bit smoother. I personally find that Excel is a fairly good tool for that if you can have a laptop next to you as you run the game (which is also good if you want to use music) since you can edit it live (i, x and o for bashing, lethal and aggravated for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:25:43-08:00","id":1008714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008056-creating-npc-sheets-in-2ed#post1008056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a side note, any idea for how one can translate 1ED characters into 2ED mechanics? Say Persephone Moore or Augusto Vidal for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used Vidal in a 2ED chronichle and I didn't find nothing special or hard to deal with. Can you give me some example about Vidal that you find hard to convert?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}